{"id": "DeYuy6WxXms", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why did Ravana lift Mount Kailash… and how did Shiva stop him with just ONE TOE? 🔱😳\n\nRavana was flying over Mount Kailash in the Pushpak Vimana when he encountered Nandi, Shiva's devoted companion. Ravana mocked him and tried to move the mountain himself.\n\nWith his TWENTY ARMS, he lifted Kailash! 💪⛰️\n\nBut Shiva didn't panic. He didn't even need to get up.\n\n**Mahadev pressed down with just ONE TOE.** 🔱\n\nSuddenly, Ravana was trapped beneath the mighty mountain. His cries echoed through the three worlds!\n\nThose cries earned him the name **RAVANA** — often associated with roaring or crying aloud.\n\nTrapped beneath Kailash, Ravana sang hymns in praise of Shiva. His devotion eventually moved Mahadev, who forgave him and granted him blessings. 🙏\n\nAnd Nandi's curse? According to a popular retelling, the monkey race Ravana had mocked would play a key role in Lanka's destruction — with Hanuman becoming one of the central figures! 🐒🔥\n\nOne mountain. One toe. One unforgettable lesson: even the mighty must learn humility.\n\n📚 Want to introduce your kids to India's rich heritage through stories?\n\nExplore the Rishi Katha Navadurga Series — Books 1–3: Shailputri, Brahmacharini & Chandraghanta.\n\n📖 Set of 3 for ₹500 \n👉 rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\n👇 SHIVA, SHANKAR, MAHESH or RUDRA — which name do you use most?\n\nSave this story and share it with a Mahadev bhakt! 🙏🔱\n\n#ShivTandavStotram #Mahadev #HarHarMahadev #Ravana #Kailash #LordShiva #Bholenath #Shiva #Ramayana #Hanuman #IndianMythology #HinduMythology #MythologyStories #RishiKatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1791791313, "like_count": 272139, "comment_count": 982, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/148.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/